-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 8, Offences relating to unlawful assembly
-- (ss 141-160). Part of the state-public group (Chapters 6-10).
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026 (inputs/PC1871.txt). Each section's text is quoted above its rules.
--
-- GENERATED by notes/state-public-gen/build.py from the hand-written ladders in
-- notes/state-public-gen/part_assembly.py; edit there and rebuild.
--
-- The shape. s 141 defines an "unlawful assembly"; s 142 a "member" of one;
-- s 146 makes every member guilty of "rioting" when force is used in
-- prosecution of the common object. Those three are predicates over ONE record,
-- `Unlawful Assembly Facts`, and the punishing sections 143, 144, 145, 147 and
-- 148 call them, so each call is one box on the ladder with its own ladder
-- stacked beneath it (the catalogue's `definitionFns`), as robbery calls theft
-- in the reference row. s 149 (constructive liability) is a predicate with no
-- charge of its own: it is "read with" the charge for the offence committed.
-- ss 150-158 each take their own record.
--
-- "unlawful assembly" (s 141) is this group's definition, which other groups
-- read (PLAN section 1): the export is `unlawful assembly within section 141`.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-state-public-common`

§ `Chapter 8 - Offences relating to unlawful assembly`

§§ `The facts of one assembly - ss 141-149`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 141-149; s 40(3)
DECLARE `Unlawful Assembly Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `an assembly of 5 or more persons`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it an assembly of 5 or more persons? (Helper: `5 or more persons` over the count.)
    `the common object is to overawe by criminal force, or show of criminal force, the Legislative or Executive Government, or any public servant in the exercise of the lawful power of such public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Was the common object of the persons composing the assembly to overawe, by criminal force (s 350) or show of criminal force, the Legislative or Executive Government, or a public servant exercising lawful power?
    `the common object is to resist the execution of any law, or of any legal process`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Was the common object to resist the execution of any law or legal process?
    `the common object is to commit any offence`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Was the common object to commit any offence? By s 40(3), "offence" in s 141 includes an offence under another law punishable with imprisonment for 6 months or upwards.
    `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to any person, to take or obtain possession of any property, or to deprive any person of the enjoyment of a right of way, or of the use of water or other incorporeal right, or to enforce any right or supposed right`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) Was the common object, by criminal force or show of criminal force, to take or obtain possession of property, to deprive anyone of a right of way, water or other incorporeal right, or to enforce a right or supposed right?
    `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to compel any person to do what he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do what he is legally entitled to do`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (e) Was the common object, by criminal force or show of criminal force, to compel anyone to do what they are not legally bound to do, or omit what they are legally entitled to do? (Explanation: an assembly lawful when it assembled may later become unlawful - answer as at the time in question.)
    `being aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 142: Was the accused aware of the facts which made the assembly an unlawful assembly?
    intentionally
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 142: Did the accused join or continue in it intentionally (s 26C)?
    `joins that assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused join the assembly?
    `continues in it`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused continue in the assembly?
    armed
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused armed with a deadly weapon, or with anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death? A wooden pole sharpened at the end is such a thing (s 144 illustration, applied to ss 148 and 158).
    `knowing that such unlawful assembly has been commanded in the manner prescribed by law to disperse`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 145: Did the accused know the unlawful assembly had been commanded, in the manner prescribed by law, to disperse?
    `force or violence is used by the unlawful assembly or by any member thereof`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 146: Was force or violence used by the unlawful assembly or by any member of it?
    `in prosecution of the common object of such assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 146: Was the force or violence used in prosecution of the assembly's common object?
    `an offence is committed by any member of the unlawful assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 149: Was an offence committed by a member of the unlawful assembly?
    `in prosecution of the common object of that assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 149: Was that offence committed in prosecution of the assembly's common object?
    `such as the members of that assembly knew to be likely to be committed in prosecution of that object`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 149: Was that offence one the members knew to be likely to be committed in prosecution of that object?
    `at the time of the committing of that offence, is a member of the same assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 149: Was the accused a member of the same assembly at the time that offence was committed?
    `the common object`
        IS A STRING @desc The common object, as it is to read after "whose common object was" - for example "to cause hurt to one Zainal bin Osman"
    `the weapon`
        IS A STRING @desc The weapon, as it is to read after "being armed with" - for example "a parang"; leave blank if not armed
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

§§ `s 141 - Unlawful assembly`

--   141. An assembly of 5 or more persons is designated an "unlawful assembly",
--   if the common object of the persons composing that assembly is -
--
--   (a) to overawe by criminal force, or show of criminal force, the Legislative
--   or Executive Government, or any public servant in the exercise of the lawful
--   power of such public servant;
--
--   (b) to resist the execution of any law, or of any legal process;
--
--   (c) to commit any offence;
--
--   (d) by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to any person, to
--   take or obtain possession of any property, or to deprive any person of the
--   enjoyment of a right of way, or of the use of water or other incorporeal
--   right of which he is in possession or enjoyment, or to enforce any right or
--   supposed right; or
--
--   (e) by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to compel any
--   person to do what he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do what he is
--   legally entitled to do.
--
--   Explanation.- An assembly which was not unlawful when it assembled may
--   subsequently become an unlawful assembly.

@export Whether an assembly is an "unlawful assembly" within section 141 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unlawful assembly within section 141` f IF
        "An"
    AND f's `an assembly of 5 or more persons`
    AND "is designated an 'unlawful assembly', if the common object of the persons composing that assembly is -"
    AND (    f's `the common object is to overawe by criminal force, or show of criminal force, the Legislative or Executive Government, or any public servant in the exercise of the lawful power of such public servant`
         OR  f's `the common object is to resist the execution of any law, or of any legal process`
         OR  f's `the common object is to commit any offence`
         OR  f's `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to any person, to take or obtain possession of any property, or to deprive any person of the enjoyment of a right of way, or of the use of water or other incorporeal right, or to enforce any right or supposed right`
         OR  f's `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to compel any person to do what he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do what he is legally entitled to do` )

§§ `s 142 - Being a member of an unlawful assembly`

--   142. Whoever, being aware of facts which render any assembly an unlawful
--   assembly, intentionally joins that assembly, or continues in it, is said to
--   be a member of an unlawful assembly.

@export Whether the accused is "a member of an unlawful assembly" within section 142 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `member of an unlawful assembly within section 142` f IF
        "Whoever, being"
    AND f's `being aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly`
    AND f's intentionally
    AND (    f's `joins that assembly`
         OR  f's `continues in it` )
    AND "is said to be a member of an"
    AND `unlawful assembly within section 141` f

§§ `s 143 - Punishment`

--   143. Whoever is a member of an unlawful assembly, shall be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with
--   both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 143
`punishment prescribed by s 143` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "143"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 143 of the Penal Code 1871 (being a member of an unlawful assembly)
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 143` f IF
        "Whoever is a"
    ... `member of an unlawful assembly within section 142` f

@export Frame a charge under section 143 of the Penal Code 1871 (being a member of an unlawful assembly), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 143` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "143" "being a member of an unlawful assembly"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 143`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 143` f)
        (CONCAT "were a member of an unlawful assembly whose common object was ", f's `the common object`, `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `an assembly of 5 or more persons`) "an assembly of 5 or more persons"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the common object is to overawe by criminal force, or show of criminal force, the Legislative or Executive Government, or any public servant in the exercise of the lawful power of such public servant` OR f's `the common object is to resist the execution of any law, or of any legal process` OR f's `the common object is to commit any offence` OR f's `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to any person, to take or obtain possession of any property, or to deprive any person of the enjoyment of a right of way, or of the use of water or other incorporeal right, or to enforce any right or supposed right` OR f's `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to compel any person to do what he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do what he is legally entitled to do`) "a common object within section 141(a) to (e)"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `being aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly`) "being aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `joins that assembly` OR f's `continues in it`) "joins that assembly, or continues in it"),
            (`missing unless` (`member of an unlawful assembly within section 142` f) "the elements of sections 141 and 142 taken together")))

§§ `s 144 - Joining an unlawful assembly armed with any deadly weapon`

--   144. Whoever, being armed with any deadly weapon, or with anything which,
--   used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, is a member of an
--   unlawful assembly shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--   extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of
--   such punishments.
--
--   Illustration A wooden pole sharpened at the end is a thing which, used as a
--   weapon of offence, is likely to cause death. This illustration is applicable
--   to sections 148 and 158.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 144
`punishment prescribed by s 144` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "144"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of such punishments"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `or with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

-- FORK SP-144: "or with any combination of such punishments" is recorded as
-- `or with both` TRUE, the nearest the shared record has.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 144 of the Penal Code 1871 (joining an unlawful assembly armed with a deadly weapon)
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 144` f IF
        "Whoever, being"
    AND f's armed
    AND "is a"
    AND `member of an unlawful assembly within section 142` f

@export Frame a charge under section 144 of the Penal Code 1871 (joining an unlawful assembly armed with a deadly weapon), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 144` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "144" "joining an unlawful assembly armed with a deadly weapon"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 144`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 144` f)
        (CONCAT "being armed with ", f's `the weapon`, ", which, used as a weapon of offence, was likely to cause death, ", (CONCAT "were a member of an unlawful assembly whose common object was ", f's `the common object`), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's armed) "armed with any deadly weapon, or with anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `an assembly of 5 or more persons`) "an assembly of 5 or more persons"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the common object is to overawe by criminal force, or show of criminal force, the Legislative or Executive Government, or any public servant in the exercise of the lawful power of such public servant` OR f's `the common object is to resist the execution of any law, or of any legal process` OR f's `the common object is to commit any offence` OR f's `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to any person, to take or obtain possession of any property, or to deprive any person of the enjoyment of a right of way, or of the use of water or other incorporeal right, or to enforce any right or supposed right` OR f's `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to compel any person to do what he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do what he is legally entitled to do`) "a common object within section 141(a) to (e)"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `being aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly`) "being aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `joins that assembly` OR f's `continues in it`) "joins that assembly, or continues in it"),
            (`missing unless` (`member of an unlawful assembly within section 142` f) "the elements of sections 141 and 142 taken together")))

§§ `s 145 - Joining or continuing in an unlawful assembly, knowing that it has been commanded to disperse`

--   145. Whoever joins or continues in an unlawful assembly, knowing that such
--   unlawful assembly has been commanded in the manner prescribed by law to
--   disperse, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
--   5 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 145
`punishment prescribed by s 145` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "145"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 145 of the Penal Code 1871 (joining or continuing in an unlawful assembly knowing it has been commanded to disperse)
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 145` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `joins that assembly`
         OR  f's `continues in it` )
    AND "in an"
    AND `unlawful assembly within section 141` f
    AND f's `knowing that such unlawful assembly has been commanded in the manner prescribed by law to disperse`

@export Frame a charge under section 145 of the Penal Code 1871 (joining or continuing in an unlawful assembly, knowing that it has been commanded to disperse), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 145` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "145" "joining or continuing in an unlawful assembly, knowing that it has been commanded to disperse"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 145`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 145` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (IF f's `joins that assembly` THEN "join" ELSE "continue in"), " an unlawful assembly whose common object was ", f's `the common object`, ", knowing that the said unlawful assembly had been commanded in the manner prescribed by law to disperse", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `joins that assembly` OR f's `continues in it`) "joins or continues in"),
            (`missing unless` (`unlawful assembly within section 141` f) "an unlawful assembly (section 141)"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing that such unlawful assembly has been commanded in the manner prescribed by law to disperse`) "knowing that such unlawful assembly has been commanded in the manner prescribed by law to disperse")))

§§ `s 146 - Force used by one member in prosecution of common object`

--   146. Whenever force or violence is used by an unlawful assembly or by any
--   member thereof, in prosecution of the common object of such assembly, every
--   member of such assembly is guilty of the offence of rioting.

@export Whether the accused is guilty of the offence of "rioting" within section 146 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `guilty of rioting` f IF
        "Whenever"
    AND f's `force or violence is used by the unlawful assembly or by any member thereof`
    AND f's `in prosecution of the common object of such assembly`
    AND "every"
    AND `member of an unlawful assembly within section 142` f
    AND "is guilty of the offence of rioting"

§§ `s 147 - Punishment for rioting`

--   147. Whoever is guilty of rioting shall be punished with imprisonment for a
--   term which may extend to 7 years and shall also be liable to caning.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 147
`punishment prescribed by s 147` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "147"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years and shall also be liable to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 147 of the Penal Code 1871 (rioting)
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 147` f IF
        "Whoever is"
    ... `guilty of rioting` f

@export Frame a charge under section 147 of the Penal Code 1871 (rioting), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 147` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "147" "rioting"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 147`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 147` f)
        (CONCAT "were a member of an unlawful assembly whose common object was ", f's `the common object`, ", and in prosecution of the common object of the said assembly, force or violence was used by the said assembly or a member of it", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`), ", and you were thereby guilty of rioting")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `an assembly of 5 or more persons`) "an assembly of 5 or more persons"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the common object is to overawe by criminal force, or show of criminal force, the Legislative or Executive Government, or any public servant in the exercise of the lawful power of such public servant` OR f's `the common object is to resist the execution of any law, or of any legal process` OR f's `the common object is to commit any offence` OR f's `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to any person, to take or obtain possession of any property, or to deprive any person of the enjoyment of a right of way, or of the use of water or other incorporeal right, or to enforce any right or supposed right` OR f's `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to compel any person to do what he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do what he is legally entitled to do`) "a common object within section 141(a) to (e)"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `being aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly`) "being aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `joins that assembly` OR f's `continues in it`) "joins that assembly, or continues in it"),
            (`missing unless` (`member of an unlawful assembly within section 142` f) "the elements of sections 141 and 142 taken together"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `force or violence is used by the unlawful assembly or by any member thereof`) "force or violence is used by the unlawful assembly or by any member thereof"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `in prosecution of the common object of such assembly`) "in prosecution of the common object of such assembly"),
            (`missing unless` (`guilty of rioting` f) "the elements of section 146 taken together")))

§§ `s 148 - Rioting, armed with a deadly weapon`

--   148. Whoever is guilty of rioting, being armed with a deadly weapon, or with
--   anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, shall
--   be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years and
--   shall also be liable to caning.
--
--   Illustration
--
--   The last section is subject to the same illustration as section 144.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 148
`punishment prescribed by s 148` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "148"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years and shall also be liable to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 148 of the Penal Code 1871 (rioting, armed with a deadly weapon)
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 148` f IF
        "Whoever is"
    AND `guilty of rioting` f
    AND "being"
    AND f's armed

@export Frame a charge under section 148 of the Penal Code 1871 (rioting, armed with a deadly weapon), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 148` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "148" "rioting, armed with a deadly weapon"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 148`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 148` f)
        (CONCAT "being armed with ", f's `the weapon`, ", which, used as a weapon of offence, was likely to cause death, ", (CONCAT "were a member of an unlawful assembly whose common object was ", f's `the common object`, ", and in prosecution of the common object of the said assembly, force or violence was used by the said assembly or a member of it", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`), ", and you were thereby guilty of rioting"))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `an assembly of 5 or more persons`) "an assembly of 5 or more persons"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the common object is to overawe by criminal force, or show of criminal force, the Legislative or Executive Government, or any public servant in the exercise of the lawful power of such public servant` OR f's `the common object is to resist the execution of any law, or of any legal process` OR f's `the common object is to commit any offence` OR f's `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to any person, to take or obtain possession of any property, or to deprive any person of the enjoyment of a right of way, or of the use of water or other incorporeal right, or to enforce any right or supposed right` OR f's `the common object is, by means of criminal force, or show of criminal force, to compel any person to do what he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do what he is legally entitled to do`) "a common object within section 141(a) to (e)"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `being aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly`) "being aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `joins that assembly` OR f's `continues in it`) "joins that assembly, or continues in it"),
            (`missing unless` (`member of an unlawful assembly within section 142` f) "the elements of sections 141 and 142 taken together"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `force or violence is used by the unlawful assembly or by any member thereof`) "force or violence is used by the unlawful assembly or by any member thereof"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `in prosecution of the common object of such assembly`) "in prosecution of the common object of such assembly"),
            (`missing unless` (`guilty of rioting` f) "the elements of section 146 taken together"),
            (`missing unless` (f's armed) "armed with any deadly weapon, or with anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death")))

§§ `s 149 - Every member of an unlawful assembly to be deemed guilty of any offence committed in prosecution of common object`

--   149. If an offence is committed by any member of an unlawful assembly in
--   prosecution of the common object of that assembly, or such as the members of
--   that assembly knew to be likely to be committed in prosecution of that
--   object, every person who, at the time of the committing of that offence, is
--   a member of the same assembly is guilty of that offence.

-- No `offence under s 149` and no charge: s 149 punishes nothing of its own. It makes
-- the member guilty of the other offence, which is charged under ITS section "read with
-- section 149" (`frame the charge read with`, pc-general). Coverage: deeming rule.
@export Whether the accused is guilty, by section 149 of the Penal Code 1871, of an offence committed by another member of the same unlawful assembly
GIVEN f IS AN `Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `guilty of that offence within section 149` f IF
        "If"
    AND f's `an offence is committed by any member of the unlawful assembly`
    AND (    f's `in prosecution of the common object of that assembly`
         OR  f's `such as the members of that assembly knew to be likely to be committed in prosecution of that object` )
    AND "every person who,"
    AND f's `at the time of the committing of that offence, is a member of the same assembly`
    AND "that is, a"
    AND `member of an unlawful assembly within section 142` f
    AND "is guilty of that offence"

§§ `s 150 - Hiring, or conniving at hiring, of persons to join an unlawful assembly`

--   150. Whoever hires, or engages, or employs, or promotes or connives at the
--   hiring, engagement, or employment of any person to join or become a member
--   of any unlawful assembly shall be punishable as a member of such unlawful
--   assembly, and for any offence which may be committed by any such person as a
--   member of such unlawful assembly, in pursuance of such hiring, engagement,
--   or employment, in the same manner as if he had been a member of such
--   unlawful assembly, or himself had committed such offence.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 150
DECLARE `Hiring for Unlawful Assembly Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `hires, or engages, or employs`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused hire, engage or employ a person?
    `promotes or connives at the hiring, engagement, or employment`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused promote, or connive at, the hiring, engagement or employment of a person?
    `of any person to join or become a member of any unlawful assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that person to join, or become a member of, an unlawful assembly?
    `unlawful assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is (or was) the assembly an unlawful assembly within section 141? (Drill-down: `unlawful assembly within section 141`.)
    `the person hired`
        IS A Person @desc The person hired, as the charge names them
    `the common object`
        IS A STRING @desc The common object of the assembly, as it is to read after "whose common object was"
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 150
`punishment prescribed by s 150` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "150"
    words                    IS "as a member of such unlawful assembly - under section 143, imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

-- FORK SP-150: s 150 makes the hirer "punishable as a member of such unlawful
-- assembly" - the punishment is s 143's, and it is recorded so. Liability for the
-- hireling's further offences "in the same manner as if he ... himself had committed
-- such offence" is charged under that offence's section read with s 150; not built here.
@export Whether the accused hires, or promotes or connives at the hiring of, a person to join an unlawful assembly, within section 150 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Hiring for Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `hires persons to join an unlawful assembly` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `hires, or engages, or employs`
         OR  f's `promotes or connives at the hiring, engagement, or employment` )
    AND f's `of any person to join or become a member of any unlawful assembly`
    AND f's `unlawful assembly`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 150 of the Penal Code 1871 (hiring persons to join an unlawful assembly)
GIVEN f IS A `Hiring for Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 150` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `hires persons to join an unlawful assembly` f

@export Frame a charge under section 150 of the Penal Code 1871 (hiring persons to join an unlawful assembly), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hiring for Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 150` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "150" "hiring persons to join an unlawful assembly"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 150`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 150` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (IF f's `hires, or engages, or employs` THEN "hire" ELSE "connive at the hiring of"), " ", `one person` (f's `the person hired`), " to join an unlawful assembly whose common object was ", f's `the common object`, `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `hires, or engages, or employs` OR f's `promotes or connives at the hiring, engagement, or employment`) "hires, engages or employs, or promotes or connives at the hiring of"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `of any person to join or become a member of any unlawful assembly`) "any person to join or become a member of any unlawful assembly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `unlawful assembly`) "an unlawful assembly (section 141)")))

§§ `s 151 - Knowingly joining or continuing in any assembly of 5 or more persons after it has been commanded to disperse`

--   151. Whoever knowingly joins or continues in any assembly of 5 or more
--   persons likely to cause a disturbance of the public peace, after such
--   assembly has been lawfully commanded to disperse, shall be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with
--   both.
--
--   Explanation.- If the assembly is an unlawful assembly within the meaning of
--   section 141, the offender will be punishable under section 145.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 151
DECLARE `Assembly Commanded to Disperse Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    knowingly
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act knowingly (s 26D)?
    joins
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused join the assembly?
    `continues in`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused continue in the assembly?
    `any assembly of 5 or more persons`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it an assembly of 5 or more persons? (Helper: `5 or more persons`.)
    `likely to cause a disturbance of the public peace`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the assembly likely to cause a disturbance of the public peace?
    `after such assembly has been lawfully commanded to disperse`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the assembly been lawfully commanded to disperse before the accused joined or continued in it?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 151
`punishment prescribed by s 151` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "151"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

-- The Explanation (an unlawful assembly is punishable under s 145) points elsewhere;
-- it does not remove the assembly from s 151, so it adds no leaf here (FORK SP-151).
@export Whether the accused knowingly joins or continues in an assembly of 5 or more persons likely to disturb the public peace after it has been lawfully commanded to disperse, within section 151 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Assembly Commanded to Disperse Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `joins an assembly commanded to disperse` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's knowingly
    AND (    f's joins
         OR  f's `continues in` )
    AND f's `any assembly of 5 or more persons`
    AND f's `likely to cause a disturbance of the public peace`
    AND f's `after such assembly has been lawfully commanded to disperse`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 151 of the Penal Code 1871 (knowingly joining or continuing in an assembly of 5 or more persons after it has been commanded to disperse)
GIVEN f IS AN `Assembly Commanded to Disperse Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 151` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `joins an assembly commanded to disperse` f

@export Frame a charge under section 151 of the Penal Code 1871 (knowingly joining or continuing in an assembly of 5 or more persons after it has been commanded to disperse), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Assembly Commanded to Disperse Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 151` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "151" "knowingly joining or continuing in an assembly of 5 or more persons after it has been commanded to disperse"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 151`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 151` f)
        (CONCAT "did knowingly ", (IF f's joins THEN "join" ELSE "continue in"), " an assembly of 5 or more persons likely to cause a disturbance of the public peace, after such assembly had been lawfully commanded to disperse", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's knowingly) "knowingly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's joins OR f's `continues in`) "joins or continues in"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `any assembly of 5 or more persons`) "an assembly of 5 or more persons"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `likely to cause a disturbance of the public peace`) "likely to cause a disturbance of the public peace"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `after such assembly has been lawfully commanded to disperse`) "after such assembly has been lawfully commanded to disperse")))

-- s 151A. [Repealed by Act 51 of 2007]

§§ `s 152 - Assaulting or obstructing public servant when suppressing riot, etc.`

--   152. Whoever assaults or threatens to assault, or obstructs or attempts to
--   obstruct, any public servant in the discharge of his duty as such public
--   servant in endeavouring to disperse an unlawful assembly or to suppress a
--   riot or an affray, or uses, or threatens or attempts to use, criminal force
--   to such public servant, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which
--   may extend to 8 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 152
DECLARE `Obstructing Riot Suppression Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    assaults
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused assault the public servant (s 351 - defined in pc-body-a; joined at integration)?
    `threatens to assault`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused threaten to assault the public servant?
    obstructs
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obstruct the public servant?
    `attempts to obstruct`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused attempt to obstruct the public servant?
    `uses criminal force to such public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused use criminal force (s 350 - defined in pc-body-a; joined at integration) on the public servant?
    `threatens or attempts to use criminal force to such public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused threaten or attempt to use criminal force on the public servant?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `in the discharge of his duty as such public servant in endeavouring to disperse an unlawful assembly or to suppress a riot or an affray`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant, in the discharge of duty as such, trying to disperse an unlawful assembly or to suppress a riot or an affray?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 152
`punishment prescribed by s 152` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "152"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 8 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 96
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused assaults, obstructs or uses criminal force on a public servant dispersing an unlawful assembly or suppressing a riot or affray, within section 152 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Obstructing Riot Suppression Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `assaults or obstructs a public servant suppressing a riot` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's assaults
         OR  f's `threatens to assault`
         OR  f's obstructs
         OR  f's `attempts to obstruct`
         OR  f's `uses criminal force to such public servant`
         OR  f's `threatens or attempts to use criminal force to such public servant` )
    AND "any"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `in the discharge of his duty as such public servant in endeavouring to disperse an unlawful assembly or to suppress a riot or an affray`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 152 of the Penal Code 1871 (assaulting or obstructing a public servant when suppressing a riot)
GIVEN f IS AN `Obstructing Riot Suppression Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 152` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `assaults or obstructs a public servant suppressing a riot` f

@export Frame a charge under section 152 of the Penal Code 1871 (assaulting or obstructing a public servant when suppressing a riot), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Obstructing Riot Suppression Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 152` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "152" "assaulting or obstructing a public servant when suppressing a riot"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 152`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 152` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", `joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's assaults) "assault"), (`included if` (f's `threatens to assault`) "threaten to assault"), (`included if` (f's obstructs) "obstruct"), (`included if` (f's `attempts to obstruct`) "attempt to obstruct"), (`included if` (f's `uses criminal force to such public servant`) "use criminal force to"), (`included if` (f's `threatens or attempts to use criminal force to such public servant`) "threaten or attempt to use criminal force to"))), " ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, in the discharge of ", `possessive pronoun` (f's `the public servant`'s pronoun), " duty as such public servant in endeavouring to disperse an unlawful assembly or to suppress a riot or an affray", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's assaults OR f's `threatens to assault` OR f's obstructs OR f's `attempts to obstruct` OR f's `uses criminal force to such public servant` OR f's `threatens or attempts to use criminal force to such public servant`) "assaults or threatens to assault, obstructs or attempts to obstruct, or uses or threatens or attempts to use criminal force"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "any public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `in the discharge of his duty as such public servant in endeavouring to disperse an unlawful assembly or to suppress a riot or an affray`) "in the discharge of his duty in endeavouring to disperse an unlawful assembly or to suppress a riot or an affray")))

§§ `s 153 - Intentionally or rashly giving provocation, with intent to cause riot`

--   153. Whoever intentionally or rashly, by doing anything which is illegal,
--   gives provocation to any person, intending or knowing it to be likely that
--   such provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed, shall,
--   if the offence of rioting is committed in consequence of such provocation,
--   be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or
--   with fine, or with both; and if the offence of rioting is not committed,
--   with imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or
--   with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 153
DECLARE `Provocation to Riot Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    intentionally
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act intentionally (s 26C)?
    rashly
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act rashly (s 26E)?
    `by doing anything which is illegal`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do something illegal (s 43)?
    `gives provocation to any person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that give provocation to anyone?
    `intending that such provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend the provocation to cause rioting (s 146)?
    `knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know the provocation was likely to cause rioting?
    `the offence of rioting is committed in consequence of such provocation`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was rioting in fact committed in consequence of the provocation? This chooses the punishment (3 years if so, 1 year if not); it is not an element.
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 153
`punishment prescribed by s 153, if the offence of rioting is committed` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "153"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 153
`punishment prescribed by s 153, if the offence of rioting is not committed` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "153"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused intentionally or rashly, by an illegal act, gives provocation intending or knowing it likely to cause rioting, within section 153 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Provocation to Riot Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `gives provocation with intent to cause riot` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's intentionally
         OR  f's rashly )
    AND f's `by doing anything which is illegal`
    AND f's `gives provocation to any person`
    AND (    f's `intending that such provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed`
         OR  f's `knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 153 of the Penal Code 1871 (giving provocation with intent to cause riot)
GIVEN f IS A `Provocation to Riot Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 153` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `gives provocation with intent to cause riot` f

@export Frame a charge under section 153 of the Penal Code 1871 (giving provocation with intent to cause riot), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Provocation to Riot Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 153` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "153" "giving provocation with intent to cause riot"
        (IF f's `the offence of rioting is committed in consequence of such provocation` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 153, if the offence of rioting is committed`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 153, if the offence of rioting is not committed`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 153` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (IF f's intentionally THEN "intentionally" ELSE "rashly"), ", by doing an illegal act, give provocation, ", (IF f's `intending that such provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed` THEN "intending" ELSE "knowing it to be likely"), " that such provocation would cause the offence of rioting to be committed", (IF f's `the offence of rioting is committed in consequence of such provocation` THEN ", and the offence of rioting was committed in consequence of such provocation" ELSE ""), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally OR f's rashly) "intentionally or rashly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `by doing anything which is illegal`) "by doing anything which is illegal"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `gives provocation to any person`) "gives provocation to any person"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending that such provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed` OR f's `knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed`) "intending or knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause rioting")))

§§ `s 154 - Owner or occupier of land on which an unlawful assembly is held`

--   154. Whenever any unlawful assembly or riot takes place, the owner or
--   occupier of the land upon which such unlawful assembly is held or such riot
--   is committed, and any person having or claiming an interest in such land,
--   shall be punishable with fine not exceeding $5,000, if he or his agent or
--   manager, knowing that such offence is being or has been committed, or having
--   reason to believe it is likely to be committed, do not give the earliest
--   notice thereof in his or their power to the principal officer at the nearest
--   police station, and do not, in the case of his or their having reason to
--   believe that it is about to be committed, use all lawful means in his or
--   their power to prevent it, and in the event of its taking place, do not use
--   all lawful means in his or their power to disperse or suppress the riot or
--   unlawful assembly.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 154
DECLARE `Land of Unlawful Assembly Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `any unlawful assembly or riot takes place`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an unlawful assembly (s 141) or riot (s 146) take place?
    `upon the land`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it held or committed upon the land in question?
    `owner or occupier of the land`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused the owner or occupier of the land?
    `any person having or claiming an interest in such land`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused have or claim an interest in the land?
    `he or his agent or manager, knowing that such offence is being or has been committed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused, or the accused's agent or manager, know the offence was being or had been committed?
    `having reason to believe it is likely to be committed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused, or the accused's agent or manager, have reason to believe (s 26) it was likely to be committed?
    `do not give the earliest notice thereof in his or their power to the principal officer at the nearest police station`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they fail to give the earliest notice in their power to the principal officer at the nearest police station?
    `do not, having reason to believe that it is about to be committed, use all lawful means in his or their power to prevent it`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having reason to believe it was about to be committed, did they fail to use all lawful means in their power to prevent it?
    `do not, in the event of its taking place, use all lawful means in his or their power to disperse or suppress the riot or unlawful assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc When it took place, did they fail to use all lawful means in their power to disperse or suppress it?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 154
`punishment prescribed by s 154` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "154"
    words                    IS "fine not exceeding $5,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

-- FORK SP-154: the three duties are cumulative, so failing ANY of them is read as
-- the offence (the section's "and do not ... and do not" lists what must all be done).
@export Whether the owner or occupier of, or a claimant to, land on which an unlawful assembly or riot takes place is punishable under section 154 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Land of Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owner or occupier fails to prevent or report an unlawful assembly` f IF
        "Whenever"
    AND f's `any unlawful assembly or riot takes place`
    AND f's `upon the land`
    AND (    f's `owner or occupier of the land`
         OR  f's `any person having or claiming an interest in such land` )
    AND "shall be punishable ... if"
    AND (    f's `he or his agent or manager, knowing that such offence is being or has been committed`
         OR  f's `having reason to believe it is likely to be committed` )
    AND (    f's `do not give the earliest notice thereof in his or their power to the principal officer at the nearest police station`
         OR  f's `do not, having reason to believe that it is about to be committed, use all lawful means in his or their power to prevent it`
         OR  f's `do not, in the event of its taking place, use all lawful means in his or their power to disperse or suppress the riot or unlawful assembly` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 154 of the Penal Code 1871 (owner or occupier of land on which an unlawful assembly is held)
GIVEN f IS A `Land of Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 154` f IF
        `owner or occupier fails to prevent or report an unlawful assembly` f

@export Frame a charge under section 154 of the Penal Code 1871 (failure by the owner or occupier of land to report or suppress an unlawful assembly or riot), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Land of Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 154` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "154" "failure by the owner or occupier of land to report or suppress an unlawful assembly or riot"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 154`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 154` f)
        (CONCAT "being ", (IF f's `owner or occupier of the land` THEN "the owner or occupier of" ELSE "a person having or claiming an interest in"), " land upon which an unlawful assembly or riot took place, did not ", `joined with` ", or did not " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's `do not give the earliest notice thereof in his or their power to the principal officer at the nearest police station`) "give the earliest notice thereof in your power to the principal officer at the nearest police station"), (`included if` (f's `do not, having reason to believe that it is about to be committed, use all lawful means in his or their power to prevent it`) "use all lawful means in your power to prevent it"), (`included if` (f's `do not, in the event of its taking place, use all lawful means in his or their power to disperse or suppress the riot or unlawful assembly`) "use all lawful means in your power to disperse or suppress it"))), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `any unlawful assembly or riot takes place` AND f's `upon the land`) "an unlawful assembly or riot takes place upon the land"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `owner or occupier of the land` OR f's `any person having or claiming an interest in such land`) "owner or occupier of the land, or a person having or claiming an interest in it"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `he or his agent or manager, knowing that such offence is being or has been committed` OR f's `having reason to believe it is likely to be committed`) "knowing that the offence is being or has been committed, or having reason to believe it is likely"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `do not give the earliest notice thereof in his or their power to the principal officer at the nearest police station` OR f's `do not, having reason to believe that it is about to be committed, use all lawful means in his or their power to prevent it` OR f's `do not, in the event of its taking place, use all lawful means in his or their power to disperse or suppress the riot or unlawful assembly`) "does not give the earliest notice, or does not use all lawful means to prevent, disperse or suppress it")))

§§ `s 155 - Liability of person for whose benefit a riot is committed`

--   155. Whenever a riot is committed for the benefit or on behalf of any person
--   who is the owner or occupier of any land respecting which such riot takes
--   place, or who claims any interest in such land, or in the subject of any
--   dispute which gave rise to the riot, or who has accepted or derived any
--   benefit therefrom, such person shall be punishable with fine, if he or his
--   agent or manager, having reason to believe that such riot was likely to be
--   committed, or that the unlawful assembly by which such riot was committed
--   was likely to be held, shall not respectively use all lawful means in his or
--   their power to prevent such riot or assembly from taking place, and for
--   suppressing and dispersing the same.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 155, 156
DECLARE `Riot for Benefit Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `a riot is committed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a riot (s 146) committed?
    `for the benefit or on behalf of the person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it committed for the benefit, or on behalf, of the person concerned?
    `owner or occupier of any land respecting which such riot takes place`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person the owner or occupier of land the riot concerned?
    `claims any interest in such land, or in the subject of any dispute which gave rise to the riot`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person claim an interest in that land, or in the subject of the dispute that gave rise to the riot?
    `has accepted or derived any benefit therefrom`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person accepted or derived any benefit from the riot?
    `the accused is that person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 155: Is the accused that person?
    `the accused is the agent or manager of that person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 156: Is the accused that person's agent or manager?
    `having reason to believe that such riot was likely to be committed, or that the unlawful assembly by which such riot was committed was likely to be held`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused (for s 155: or the accused's agent or manager) have reason to believe (s 26) the riot, or the unlawful assembly that committed it, was likely?
    `shall not use all lawful means in his or their power to prevent such riot or assembly from taking place, and for suppressing and dispersing the same`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they fail to use all lawful means in their power to prevent the riot or assembly, and to suppress and disperse it?
    `the person`
        IS A Person @desc The person for whose benefit the riot was committed, as the charge names them (for s 156)
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 155
`punishment prescribed by s 155` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "155"
    words                    IS "fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether a riot is committed for the benefit or on behalf of an owner, occupier, claimant or beneficiary, within sections 155 and 156 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Riot for Benefit Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `riot committed for the benefit of that person` f IF
        "Whenever"
    AND f's `a riot is committed`
    AND f's `for the benefit or on behalf of the person`
    AND (    f's `owner or occupier of any land respecting which such riot takes place`
         OR  f's `claims any interest in such land, or in the subject of any dispute which gave rise to the riot`
         OR  f's `has accepted or derived any benefit therefrom` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 155 of the Penal Code 1871 (liability of the person for whose benefit a riot is committed)
GIVEN f IS A `Riot for Benefit Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 155` f IF
        `riot committed for the benefit of that person` f
    AND "such person"
    AND f's `the accused is that person`
    AND "shall be punishable with fine, if he or his agent or manager,"
    AND f's `having reason to believe that such riot was likely to be committed, or that the unlawful assembly by which such riot was committed was likely to be held`
    AND f's `shall not use all lawful means in his or their power to prevent such riot or assembly from taking place, and for suppressing and dispersing the same`

@export Frame a charge under section 155 of the Penal Code 1871 (failure by the person for whose benefit a riot is committed to prevent it), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Riot for Benefit Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 155` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "155" "failure by the person for whose benefit a riot is committed to prevent it"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 155`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 155` f)
        (CONCAT "being a person for whose benefit a riot was committed, and having reason to believe that such riot was likely to be committed, did not use all lawful means in your power to prevent such riot from taking place, and for suppressing and dispersing the same", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (`riot committed for the benefit of that person` f) "a riot committed for the benefit or on behalf of an owner, occupier, claimant or beneficiary"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the accused is that person`) "the accused is that person"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `having reason to believe that such riot was likely to be committed, or that the unlawful assembly by which such riot was committed was likely to be held`) "having reason to believe that such riot or assembly was likely"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `shall not use all lawful means in his or their power to prevent such riot or assembly from taking place, and for suppressing and dispersing the same`) "not using all lawful means to prevent, suppress and disperse it")))

§§ `s 156 - Liability of agent of owner or occupier for whose benefit a riot is committed`

--   156. Whenever a riot is committed for the benefit or on behalf of any person
--   who is the owner or occupier of any land respecting which such riot takes
--   place, or who claims any interest in such land, or in the subject of any
--   dispute which gave rise to the riot, or who has accepted or derived any
--   benefit therefrom, the agent or manager of such person shall be punishable
--   with fine, if such agent or manager, having reason to believe that such riot
--   was likely to be committed, or that the unlawful assembly by which such riot
--   was committed was likely to be held, shall not use all lawful means in his
--   power to prevent such riot or assembly from taking place, and for
--   suppressing and dispersing the same.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 156
`punishment prescribed by s 156` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "156"
    words                    IS "fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 156 of the Penal Code 1871 (liability of the agent of the person for whose benefit a riot is committed)
GIVEN f IS A `Riot for Benefit Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 156` f IF
        `riot committed for the benefit of that person` f
    AND "the"
    AND f's `the accused is the agent or manager of that person`
    AND "shall be punishable with fine, if such agent or manager,"
    AND f's `having reason to believe that such riot was likely to be committed, or that the unlawful assembly by which such riot was committed was likely to be held`
    AND f's `shall not use all lawful means in his or their power to prevent such riot or assembly from taking place, and for suppressing and dispersing the same`

@export Frame a charge under section 156 of the Penal Code 1871 (failure by the agent or manager of the person for whose benefit a riot is committed to prevent it), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Riot for Benefit Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 156` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "156" "failure by the agent or manager of the person for whose benefit a riot is committed to prevent it"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 156`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 156` f)
        (CONCAT "being the agent or manager of ", `one person` (f's `the person`), ", for whose benefit a riot was committed, and having reason to believe that such riot was likely to be committed, did not use all lawful means in your power to prevent such riot from taking place, and for suppressing and dispersing the same", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (`riot committed for the benefit of that person` f) "a riot committed for the benefit or on behalf of an owner, occupier, claimant or beneficiary"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the accused is the agent or manager of that person`) "the accused is the agent or manager of that person"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `having reason to believe that such riot was likely to be committed, or that the unlawful assembly by which such riot was committed was likely to be held`) "having reason to believe that such riot or assembly was likely"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `shall not use all lawful means in his or their power to prevent such riot or assembly from taking place, and for suppressing and dispersing the same`) "not using all lawful means to prevent, suppress and disperse it")))

§§ `s 157 - Harbouring persons hired for an unlawful assembly`

--   157. Whoever harbours, receives or assembles in any house or premises in his
--   occupation or charge, or under his control, any persons, knowing that such
--   persons have been hired, engaged or employed, or are about to be hired,
--   engaged or employed, to join or become members of an unlawful assembly, with
--   the intention of permitting or facilitating them to join or become members
--   of an unlawful assembly, or of screening them or any of them from
--   punishment, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend
--   to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 157
DECLARE `Harbouring Hired Persons Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `harbours, receives or assembles any persons`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused harbour, receive or assemble persons? ("Harbour" is defined only for Chapters 6 and 7 (ss 130A, 140A); here it has its ordinary meaning - FORK SP-157.)
    `in any house or premises in his occupation or charge, or under his control`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in a house or premises in the accused's occupation or charge, or under the accused's control?
    `knowing that such persons have been hired, engaged or employed, or are about to be hired, engaged or employed, to join or become members of an unlawful assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know those persons had been, or were about to be, hired, engaged or employed to join an unlawful assembly?
    `with the intention of permitting or facilitating them to join or become members of an unlawful assembly`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to permit or facilitate their joining the unlawful assembly?
    `with the intention of screening them or any of them from punishment`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to screen them, or any of them, from punishment?
    `the premises`
        IS A STRING @desc The house or premises, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 157
`punishment prescribed by s 157` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "157"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused harbours persons hired for an unlawful assembly, within section 157 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Hired Persons Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harbours persons hired for an unlawful assembly` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `harbours, receives or assembles any persons`
    AND f's `in any house or premises in his occupation or charge, or under his control`
    AND f's `knowing that such persons have been hired, engaged or employed, or are about to be hired, engaged or employed, to join or become members of an unlawful assembly`
    AND (    f's `with the intention of permitting or facilitating them to join or become members of an unlawful assembly`
         OR  f's `with the intention of screening them or any of them from punishment` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 157 of the Penal Code 1871 (harbouring persons hired for an unlawful assembly)
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Hired Persons Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 157` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `harbours persons hired for an unlawful assembly` f

@export Frame a charge under section 157 of the Penal Code 1871 (harbouring persons hired for an unlawful assembly), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Harbouring Hired Persons Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 157` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "157" "harbouring persons hired for an unlawful assembly"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 157`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 157` f)
        (CONCAT "did harbour, in ", f's `the premises`, ", under your control, persons, knowing that such persons had been hired to join an unlawful assembly, with the intention of ", (IF f's `with the intention of permitting or facilitating them to join or become members of an unlawful assembly` THEN "permitting or facilitating them to join such unlawful assembly" ELSE "screening them from punishment"), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `harbours, receives or assembles any persons`) "harbours, receives or assembles any persons"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `in any house or premises in his occupation or charge, or under his control`) "in any house or premises in his occupation or charge, or under his control"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing that such persons have been hired, engaged or employed, or are about to be hired, engaged or employed, to join or become members of an unlawful assembly`) "knowing that such persons have been or are about to be hired to join an unlawful assembly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of permitting or facilitating them to join or become members of an unlawful assembly` OR f's `with the intention of screening them or any of them from punishment`) "with the intention of permitting or facilitating their joining, or of screening them from punishment")))

§§ `s 158 - Being hired to take part in an unlawful assembly or riot`

--   158. Whoever is engaged or hired, or offers or attempts to be hired or
--   engaged, to do or assist in doing any of the acts specified in section 141,
--   shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years,
--   or with fine, or with both; and whoever, being so engaged or hired as
--   aforesaid, goes armed, or engages or offers to go armed, with any deadly
--   weapon, or with anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to
--   cause death, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend
--   to 5 years, or with fine, or with both.
--
--   Illustration
--
--   The last section is subject to the same illustration as section 144.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 158
DECLARE `Hired for Unlawful Assembly Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `is engaged or hired`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused engaged or hired?
    `offers or attempts to be hired or engaged`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused offer, or attempt, to be hired or engaged?
    `to do or assist in doing any of the acts specified in section 141`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it to do, or assist in doing, any of the acts specified in section 141 (the common objects (a) to (e))?
    `goes armed, or engages or offers to go armed, with any deadly weapon, or with anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused, being so hired, go armed - or engage or offer to go armed - with a deadly weapon, or anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death (s 144 illustration: a sharpened wooden pole)? This chooses the higher punishment.
    `the acts`
        IS A STRING @desc The acts the accused was hired to do, as they are to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 158
`punishment prescribed by s 158` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "158"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 158
`punishment prescribed by s 158, where the person so hired goes armed` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "158"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused is hired, or offers to be hired, to do any of the acts specified in section 141, within section 158 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Hired for Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is hired to take part in an unlawful assembly` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's `is engaged or hired`
         OR  f's `offers or attempts to be hired or engaged` )
    AND f's `to do or assist in doing any of the acts specified in section 141`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 158 of the Penal Code 1871 (being hired to take part in an unlawful assembly or riot)
GIVEN f IS A `Hired for Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 158` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `is hired to take part in an unlawful assembly` f

@export Frame a charge under section 158 of the Penal Code 1871 (being hired to take part in an unlawful assembly or riot), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hired for Unlawful Assembly Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 158` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "158" "being hired to take part in an unlawful assembly or riot"
        (IF f's `goes armed, or engages or offers to go armed, with any deadly weapon, or with anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 158, where the person so hired goes armed`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 158`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 158` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (IF f's `is engaged or hired` THEN "engage to be hired" ELSE "offer to be hired"), " to do ", f's `the acts`, ", being acts specified in section 141 of the Penal Code 1871", (IF f's `goes armed, or engages or offers to go armed, with any deadly weapon, or with anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death` THEN ", and, being so hired, did go armed with a weapon of offence likely to cause death" ELSE ""), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `is engaged or hired` OR f's `offers or attempts to be hired or engaged`) "is engaged or hired, or offers or attempts to be"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `to do or assist in doing any of the acts specified in section 141`) "to do or assist in doing any of the acts specified in section 141")))

-- s 159. [Repealed by Act 51 of 2007]
-- s 160. [Repealed by Act 51 of 2007]
